<!-- Inline Editor Section -->
<div id="post-by-editor" class="mt-16 mb-4 md:mb-8 mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
  <h2 class="source-serif text-center font-semibold my-8 text-3xl md:text-4xl tracking-tight">A wonderful editor for writing, built in</h2>

  <p class="md:text-xl leading-relaxed my-5">
    Pagecord has a wonderful online editor for writing posts in your browser, or on your phone. Use Markdown syntax, add formatting, images, galleries, tables, colours, and code blocks with syntax highlighting.
  </p>

  <%= image_tag home_image_path("home/rich-text-editor.webp", width: 1600, quality: 90),
    srcset: home_image_srcset("home/rich-text-editor.webp", widths: [ 800, 1600 ], quality: 88),
    sizes: "(min-width: 56rem) 54rem, 100vw",
    alt: "A screenshot of Pagecord's rich text editor",
    width: "1600",
    height: "967" %>
</div>

<!-- Post by Email Section -->
<div id="post-by-email" class="mt-16 mb-4 md:mb-8 mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
  <h2 class="source-serif text-center font-semibold my-8 text-3xl md:text-4xl tracking-tight">Post by sending an email</h2>

  <p class="md:text-xl leading-relaxed my-5">
    Email is already on every device you use. Send a message to your private Pagecord address and it becomes a post on your blog.
  </p>

  <p class="md:text-xl leading-relaxed my-5">
  Text formatting, images and links all look great!
  </p>
  <%= image_tag home_image_path("home/gmail-compose.webp", width: 1600, quality: 90),
        srcset: home_image_srcset("home/gmail-compose.webp", widths: [ 800, 1600 ], quality: 88),
        sizes: "(min-width: 56rem) 54rem, 100vw",
        alt: "Screenshot of composing a post in Gmail",
        width: "1600",
        height: "967" %>
</div>

<!-- Obsidian and API Section -->
<div id="obsidian-api" class="mt-16 mb-4 md:mb-8 mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
  <h2 class="source-serif text-center font-semibold my-8 text-3xl md:text-4xl tracking-tight">Publish from Obsidian, iA Writer, or your own scripts</h2>

  <p class="md:text-xl leading-relaxed my-5">
  The <a href="https://help.pagecord.com/obsidian" class="font-medium underline">official Pagecord Obsidian plugin</a> publishes selected notes straight to your blog. If you prefer <a href="https://help.pagecord.com/micropub#using-ia-writer" class="font-medium underline">iA Writer</a>, Pagecord has you covered. Or you can use the <a href="https://help.pagecord.com/api" class="font-medium underline">Pagecord API</a> and <a href="https://help.pagecord.com/pagecord-cli" class="font-medium underline">CLI</a> to publish from Shortcuts, scripts, local folders, or any workflow that already works for you.
  </p>

  <%= image_tag home_image_path("home/obsidian.webp", width: 1600, quality: 90),
        srcset: home_image_srcset("home/obsidian.webp", widths: [ 800, 1600 ], quality: 88),
        sizes: "(min-width: 56rem) 54rem, 100vw",
        alt: "Screenshot of the composing a post in Obsidian",
        width: "1600",
        height: "1609" %>
</div>

<!-- Newsletter Section -->
<div id="newsletter" class="mt-16 mb-4 md:mb-8 mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
  <h2 class="source-serif text-center font-semibold my-8 text-3xl md:text-4xl tracking-tight">Your blog posts are easy to follow</h2>

  <p class="md:text-xl leading-relaxed my-5">
    Every Pagecord blog has RSS, but not everyone uses it. With Pagecord Premium, readers can subscribe to your blog by email and receive an automatic <strong>weekly digest</strong>. If you prefer, you can send posts individually instead, on your schedule.
  </p>

  <%= image_tag home_image_path("home/weekly-digest.webp", width: 1600, quality: 90),
    srcset: home_image_srcset("home/weekly-digest.webp", widths: [ 800, 1600 ], quality: 88),
    sizes: "(min-width: 56rem) 54rem, 100vw",
    alt: "A screenshot of Apple Mail with a weekly digest email",
    width: "1600",
    height: "967" %>
</div>

<!-- Comments Section -->
<div id="comments" class="mt-16 mb-4 md:mb-8 mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
  <h2 class="source-serif text-center font-semibold my-8 text-3xl md:text-4xl tracking-tight">Host a conversation with comments</h2>

  <p class="md:text-xl leading-relaxed my-5">
    With Pagecord Premium you can enable comments on your posts. Readers leave a name and a message: no account needed, no email address revealed. You can post a reply to any of them.
  </p>

  <p class="md:text-xl leading-relaxed my-5">
    Comments won't appear until you approve them, and spam is filtered out before it reaches you.
  </p>

  <%= image_tag home_image_path("home/comments.webp", width: 1600, quality: 90),
    srcset: home_image_srcset("home/comments.webp", widths: [ 800, 1600 ], quality: 88),
    sizes: "(min-width: 56rem) 54rem, 100vw",
    alt: "A screenshot of comments on a Pagecord blog post",
    width: "1600",
    height: "922" %>
</div>

<!-- Analytics Section -->
<div id="analytics" class="mt-16 mb-4 md:mb-8 mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
  <h2 class="source-serif text-center font-semibold my-8 text-3xl md:text-4xl tracking-tight">Privacy-respecting analytics built in</h2>

  <p class="md:text-xl leading-relaxed my-5">
  It's nice to know how many visitors your blog gets, and where they come from, but you shouldn't have to add costly 3rd party tracking scripts.</p>
  <p class="md:text-xl leading-relaxed my-5">
  Pagecord Premium has simple, privacy-first analytics built in. And if you would rather not know, you can turn it all off.
  </p>

  <%= image_tag home_image_path("home/analytics.webp", width: 1600, quality: 90),
    srcset: home_image_srcset("home/analytics.webp", widths: [ 800, 1600 ], quality: 88),
    sizes: "(min-width: 56rem) 54rem, 100vw",
    alt: "A screenshot of Pagecord's page view analytics page",
    width: "1600",
    height: "964" %>
</div>
